cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use pystreme, please cite it, and cite STREME, whose algorithm it
  reimplements (see references).
title: pystreme
abstract: >-
  GPU-batched, in-process reimplementation of the STREME algorithm for de novo
  motif discovery from peak sets. Unofficial; not affiliated with the MEME
  Suite. Code written with Claude Code (Anthropic); design and validation by
  the author.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mindel
    given-names: Vladimir
    alias: vmindel
repository-code: "https://github.com/vmindel/pystreme"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22749207
date-released: 2026-09-14
keywords:
  - motif discovery
  - STREME
  - ChIP-seq
  - ChEC-seq
  - GPU
references:
  - type: article
    title: "STREME: accurate and versatile sequence motif discovery"
    authors:
      - family-names: Bailey
        given-names: Timothy L.
    journal: Bioinformatics
    volume: 37
    issue: 18
    start: 2834
    end: 2840
    year: 2021
    doi: 10.1093/bioinformatics/btab203
